IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- SCHEDULE 3A -- EXCLUDED TRUSTS (S.I. 2017/692, lines 3082-3205 of the plain-text rendering, which is not the
-- official text and is not verified against it).
--
-- WHAT IT IS FOR.  Regulations 42 (line 1331), 45(10A) (line 1463) and 45ZA(2) (lines 1509-1510) describe the trusts they reach as trusts that are "not a trust listed in
-- Schedule 3A (excluded trusts)" (or, in regulation 45(10A), "is not an EEA registered trust or a trust listed in Schedule 3A").  This module is that Schedule: SEAM S-18, answered here for
-- part mlr2.
--
-- THE SHAPE OF THE SCHEDULE AND OF THIS MODULE.  Each paragraph of the Schedule describes one kind of trust.
-- Each has one function here whose inputs are the facts of that paragraph.  A paragraph is read in two parts: its HEAD (what the trust is:
-- "A trust of jointly held property") and its TRIGGERS (the conditions the text states in its own words: "where", "if", a period, "only").
-- The answer is JUST TRUE when the head and every trigger hold; JUST FALSE when the head holds and a trigger does not (Meng's rulings of 2026-11-05:
-- a period the text fixes in its own words, and a "where" condition, answer JUST FALSE when unmet, like "if"; and a paragraph closed by "only"
-- answers JUST FALSE for a case outside it); and NOTHING when the head itself is not met, because the paragraph is one entry in a list that does not say "only"
-- (FORK S3A-F2).  A paragraph whose whole description is a relative clause ("A trust holding sums or assets of a pension scheme which is a registered
-- pension scheme") has no trigger, so it answers NOTHING outside the description: paragraphs 1, 2, 3, 4(3), 5, 9B, 10(1)(a) and (b), 11, 16 to 16+6, 23, 23A(1) and the amount in 6(a).  The Schedule's own definitions ("relevant account", "authorised Part 4A person", "estate", "segregating entity",
-- "relevant supervised person", written with "means") answer JUST FALSE outside them, and the paragraphs that use one pass its no through (paragraphs 6A(1), 10(1)(c), 12, 13).
-- Paragraph 23A(2) ("This paragraph does not apply") is a flat negative: JUST FALSE.
-- The functions are gathered at the end by hand (ruling E1, option B) into `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`, which is the seam's answer.
-- That function answers JUST TRUE if any paragraph does; NOTHING if a paragraph would say JUST TRUE were an answer still unknown (the two relevant-supervised-person
-- inputs of paragraphs 12 and 13) to turn out yes; and otherwise JUST FALSE, because the Schedule is read as the list to which the term "a trust listed in
-- Schedule 3A (excluded trusts)" of regulations 42, 45 and 45ZA is handed, so that a trust within no paragraph is not listed (assumed, not ruled: FORK S3A-F8).
--
-- THE RENDERING PRINTS SOME PARAGRAPH NUMBERS AND NOT OTHERS (FORK S3A-F1).  Paragraphs 1 to 6, 6A, 7, 9, 9B, 10 to 16,
-- 23, 23A and 24 are printed with a number (and a heading); the rest are printed as bare paragraphs after the
-- number above them.  The bare paragraphs are labelled here by position: `sch 3A para 1+1` is the first
-- unnumbered paragraph printed after paragraph 1; `7+1` and `7+2` the first and second after paragraph 7; `9+1`
-- the one after paragraph 9; `16+1` to `16+6` the six after paragraph 16.  The labels claim no official number.
--
-- BORROWED FACTS.  Almost every paragraph turns on a term of another Act (the Finance Act 2004, the Trustee Act
-- 1925, the Mental Capacity Act 2005, FSMA, the Freedom of Information Acts, ...).  Each is a plain BOOLEAN fact
-- the caller states; none is looked up.  The two borrowed figures of paragraph 6 are inputs as well: the value
-- limit is the Schedule's own (100) and the date regulation 42(2)(iii) comes into force is NOT in the rendering
-- (PLAN.md section 5.5), so it is an input DATE (FORK S3A-F3).
--
-- TWO YEARS FROM A DEATH.  Five paragraphs (1+1, 7, 7+1, 7+2, 9+1) say "less than two years has passed since that
-- person's death".  `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` builds the second anniversary from
-- the actual date with `Date day month year` (DATE_YEAR plus 2); a death on 29 February has its second
-- anniversary on 1 March under the Date convention (FORK S3A-F4).
--
-- TWO MORE READINGS.  Paragraph 4(2)(a) ends "where that policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under sub-paragraph (1)"; the "where" clause is read as
-- attaching to limb (a) alone, so a policy that also pays for healthcare under limb (b) needs no such coincidence (FORK S3A-F5).  Paragraph 13 reads "points 2, 3, 6, 7 or 8 of ... Schedule 2": the
-- rendering replaces the words before "Schedule 2" with an ellipsis, so the instrument whose Schedule 2 is meant is not shown (PLAN.md 5.3 takes it as Schedule 2 to these Regulations, whose items the
-- core names in `Listed activity` without numbering them); the points cannot be computed from the core, so the whole description is one BOOLEAN fact the caller states (FORK S3A-F6).
--
-- READINGS ADDED BY THE RULINGS OF 2026-11-05 (each assumed, not ruled, and each in the fork register of NOTES.md).  Paragraph 6(b), "was created before the date on which regulation
-- 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force", is a date the text fixes in its own words, read like a period: a trust created on or after it answers JUST FALSE whatever its value (FORK S3A-F3).
-- Paragraph 10(1)(c) turns on "segregating entity", defined with "means"; when the trust has one of the purposes of (c) and the entity is not a segregating entity, the definition's no
-- passes through and the paragraph answers JUST FALSE, but when neither purpose is present it stays NOTHING, because (a) and (b) are separate descriptions that the definition does not touch (FORK S3A-F7).
-- Paragraph 15 says "where the purpose of the trust is to hold the legal title ... until the time when the procedure ... is completed": the "where" is read as a condition of the description, not
-- as a bar that a date lifts (FORK S3A-F9).  The paragraph 23 phrase "to carry out its functions" states a purpose, not a condition, so it stays NOTHING.

-- src:3082 | SCHEDULE 3A — Excluded Trusts
§ `Schedule 3A -- Excluded Trusts`

-- The kinds of asset named in paragraph 23A(3), and a catch-all for the open list.
DECLARE `sch 3A kind of asset` IS ONE OF
    `sch 3A a work of art`
    `sch 3A an antique`
    `sch 3A a collectible`
    `sch 3A jewellery`
    `sch 3A another non-financial asset capable of increasing in value over time`
    `sch 3A an asset of another kind`

-- src:3083 | 1 Legislative Trusts
-- src:3084 | A trust imposed or required by an enactment.
@ref sch 3A para 1 (src:3083-3084)
GIVEN `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 1 the trust is a legislative trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3085 | A trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 of this Schedule where—
-- src:3086 | (a) the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925;
-- src:3087 | (b) the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees; and
-- src:3088 | (c) less than two years has passed since that person’s death.
@ref sch 3A para 1+1 (src:3085-3088)
GIVEN `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the death of that trustee` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1`
           AND `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925`
           AND `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees`
           AND `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of that trustee` `the date for which the trust is being tested`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1`
           AND (NOT (    `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925`
                     AND `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees`
                     AND `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of that trustee` `the date for which the trust is being tested`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 of this Schedule where— (a) the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925; (b) the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees; and (c) less than two years has passed since that person's death"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


@ref sch 3A para 1+1(c) (src:3088)
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` MEANS
        `the date for which the trust is being tested` AT LEAST `the date of the death`
    AND `the date for which the trust is being tested` LESS THAN (Date (DATE_DAY `the date of the death`) (DATE_MONTH `the date of the death`) (DATE_YEAR `the date of the death` PLUS 2))

-- src:3089 | 2 Trusts imposed by court order
-- src:3090 | A trust created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal.
@ref sch 3A para 2 (src:3089-3090)
GIVEN `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 2 the trust is a trust imposed by court order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3091 | 3 Pension scheme trusts
-- src:3092 | A trust holding sums or assets of a pension scheme which is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004.
@ref sch 3A para 3 (src:3091-3092)
GIVEN `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 3 the trust is a pension scheme trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme`
            AND `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3093 | 4 Trusts of insurance policies
-- src:3094 | (1) A trust of a life policy paying out only—
-- src:3095 | (a) on the death, terminal or critical illness, or permanent or temporary disablement of the person assured; or
-- src:3096 | (b) to meet the cost of healthcare services provided to the person assured.
@ref sch 3A para 4(1) (src:3093-3096)
GIVEN `the trust is of a life policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 4(1) the trust is a trust of a life policy paying out only on the listed events or for healthcare` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust is of a life policy`
           AND (NOT `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust is of a life policy`
           AND (NOT (NOT `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust of a life policy paying out only— (a) on the death, terminal or critical illness, or permanent or temporary disablement of the person assured; or (b) to meet the cost of healthcare services provided to the person assured"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3097 | (2) A trust of an insurance policy paying out only—
-- src:3098 | (a) on the temporary disablement of the person assured, where that policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under sub-paragraph (1); or
-- src:3099 | (b) to meet the cost of healthcare services provided to the person assured.
@ref sch 3A para 4(2) (src:3097-3099)
GIVEN `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 4(2) the trust is a trust of an insurance policy paying out only on temporary disablement or for healthcare` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust is of an insurance policy`
           AND (NOT `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)`)
           AND (    (NOT `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured`)
                 OR `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust is of an insurance policy`
           AND (NOT (    (NOT `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)`)
                     AND (    (NOT `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured`)
                 OR `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)`)))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust of an insurance policy paying out only— (a) on the temporary disablement of the person assured, where that policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under sub-paragraph (1); or (b) to meet the cost of healthcare services provided to the person assured"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3100 | (3) A trust of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy.
@ref sch 3A para 4(3) (src:3100)
GIVEN `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 4(3) the trust is a trust of the death benefits of a retirement policy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3101 | 5 Charitable trusts
-- src:3102 | A trust for charitable purposes which—
-- src:3103 | (a) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, is registered as a charity; or
-- src:3104 | (b) in England and Wales, is registered as a charity or not required to register by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011.
@ref sch 3A para 5 (src:3101-3104)
GIVEN `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
      `the trust is registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust is for charitable purposes`
           AND (    (    (    `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` EQUALS `Scotland`
                          OR `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` EQUALS `Northern Ireland`)
                     AND `the trust is registered as a charity`)
                 OR (    `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` EQUALS `England and Wales`
                     AND (    `the trust is registered as a charity`
                           OR `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011`)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3105 | 6 Pilot trusts
-- src:3106 | A trust which—
-- src:3107 | (a) holds property with a value not exceeding £100, and
-- src:3108 | (b) was created before the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force.
@ref sch 3A para 6 (src:3105-3108)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3A para 6(a) the value limit in pounds` MEANS 100

@ref sch 3A para 6 (src:3105-3108)
GIVEN `the value of the property the trust holds` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the trust was created` IS A DATE
      `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the value of the property the trust holds` AT MOST `sch 3A para 6(a) the value limit in pounds`
           AND `the date the trust was created` LESS THAN `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT (`the date the trust was created` LESS THAN `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) was created before the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force" is a date the text fixes in its own words, read like a period (assumed, not ruled: FORK S3A-F3)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3109 | 6A Bank accounts for minors etc
-- src:3110 | (1) A trust which is created as a requirement of opening a relevant account for the sole benefit of—
-- src:3111 | (a) a person under the age of 18;
-- src:3112 | (b) a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005;
-- src:3113 | (c) a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000; or
-- src:3114 | (d) a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person’s property and affairs, by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986.
@ref sch 3A para 6A(1) (src:3109-3114)
GIVEN `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 6A(1) the trust is created as a requirement of opening a relevant account for the sole benefit of a minor or an incapable person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account`
           AND `sch 3A para 6A(2) the account is a relevant account` `the account consists only of a sum of money` `the person is an authorised person` `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (    `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18`
                 OR `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005`
                 OR `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000`
                 OR `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account`
           AND `sch 3A para 6A(2) the account is a relevant account` `the account consists only of a sum of money` `the person is an authorised person` `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant account' means an account, consisting only of a sum of money, held with an authorised Part 4A person carrying on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits)": the term the head uses is defined with "means", so its no passes through the paragraph
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3115 | (2) In this paragraph—
-- src:3116 | “relevant account” means an account, consisting only of a sum of money, held with an authorised Part 4A person carrying on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001;
-- src:3117 | “authorised Part 4A person” means an authorised person who has a Part 4A permission, within the meaning given to that term in section 55A(5) of FSMA, to carry on that specified activity.
@ref sch 3A para 6A(2) (src:3115-3117)
GIVEN `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 6A(2) the account is a relevant account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the account consists only of a sum of money`
           AND `sch 3A para 6A(2) the person is an authorised Part 4A person` `the person is an authorised person` `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant account' means an account, consisting only of a sum of money, held with an authorised Part 4A person carrying on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits)"


@ref sch 3A para 6A(2) (src:3117)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 6A(2) the person is an authorised Part 4A person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the person is an authorised person`
           AND `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'authorised Part 4A person' means an authorised person who has a Part 4A permission ... to carry on that specified activity"


-- src:3118 | 7 Trusts having effect on death
-- src:3119 | (1) A trust effected by will where—
-- src:3120 | (a) the trust is holding only the property comprised in a person’s estate on death, and
-- src:3121 | (b) less than two years has passed since that person’s death.
-- src:3122 | (2) In this paragraph, a person’s “estate” means the aggregate of all the property to which that person is beneficially entitled.
@ref sch 3A para 7(1) (src:3118-3122)
GIVEN `the trust was effected by will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was beneficially entitled to all the property the trust holds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the death of the person` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 7(1) the trust is a trust effected by will holding only the estate within two years of the death` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust was effected by will`
           AND `sch 3A para 7(2) the property is comprised in a person's estate` `the person was beneficially entitled to all the property the trust holds` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of the person` `the date for which the trust is being tested`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust was effected by will`
           AND (NOT (    `sch 3A para 7(2) the property is comprised in a person's estate` `the person was beneficially entitled to all the property the trust holds` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                     AND `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of the person` `the date for which the trust is being tested`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust effected by will where— (a) the trust is holding only the property comprised in a person's estate on death, and (b) less than two years has passed since that person's death"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


@ref sch 3A para 7(2) (src:3122)
GIVEN `the person is beneficially entitled to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 7(2) the property is comprised in a person's estate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is beneficially entitled to the property`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person's 'estate' means the aggregate of all the property to which that person is beneficially entitled"


-- src:3123 | A trust where—
-- src:3124 | (a) the trust is holding only benefits received on the death of the person assured under a policy within paragraph 4, and
-- src:3125 | (b) less than two years has passed since that person’s death.
@ref sch 3A para 7+1 (src:3123-3125)
GIVEN `the trust holds only benefits received on the death of the person assured under a policy within paragraph 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the death of the person` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 7+1 the trust holds only death benefits of a policy within paragraph 4 within two years of the death` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust holds only benefits received on the death of the person assured under a policy within paragraph 4`
           AND `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of the person` `the date for which the trust is being tested`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust where— (a) the trust is holding only benefits received on the death of the person assured under a policy within paragraph 4, and (b) less than two years has passed since that person's death"


-- src:3126 | (1) A trust created under a deed or instrument which—
-- src:3127 | (a) varies any of the dispositions of property comprised in a person’s (“P’s”) estate on death, and
-- src:3128 | (b) was made by the persons or any of the persons who benefit or would benefit from the dispositions,
-- src:3129 | where less than two years has passed since P’s death.
-- src:3130 | (2) In this paragraph, a person’s “estate” means the aggregate of all property to which that person is beneficially entitled.
@ref sch 3A para 7+2 (src:3126-3130)
GIVEN `the trust was created under a deed or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed or instrument varies any of the dispositions of property comprised in the estate on death of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed or instrument was made by the persons or any of the persons who benefit or would benefit from the dispositions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the death of the person` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 7+2 the trust is created under a deed or instrument varying dispositions of an estate within two years of the death` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust was created under a deed or instrument`
           AND `the deed or instrument varies any of the dispositions of property comprised in the estate on death of a person`
           AND `the deed or instrument was made by the persons or any of the persons who benefit or would benefit from the dispositions`
           AND `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of the person` `the date for which the trust is being tested`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust was created under a deed or instrument`
           AND `the deed or instrument varies any of the dispositions of property comprised in the estate on death of a person`
           AND `the deed or instrument was made by the persons or any of the persons who benefit or would benefit from the dispositions`
           AND (NOT `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of the person` `the date for which the trust is being tested`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust created under a deed or instrument which ... where less than two years has passed since P's death"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


@ref sch 3A para 7+2(2) (src:3130)
GIVEN `the person is beneficially entitled to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 7+2(2) the property is comprised in P's estate` MEANS
    `sch 3A para 7(2) the property is comprised in a person's estate` `the person is beneficially entitled to the property`

-- src:3131 | 9 Co-ownership
-- src:3132 | A trust of jointly held property where the trustees and the beneficiaries are the same persons.
@ref sch 3A para 9 (src:3131-3132)
GIVEN `the trust is of jointly held property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees and the beneficiaries are the same persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 9 the trust is a co-ownership trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust is of jointly held property`
           AND `the trustees and the beneficiaries are the same persons`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust is of jointly held property`
           AND (NOT `the trustees and the beneficiaries are the same persons`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust of jointly held property where the trustees and the beneficiaries are the same persons"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3133 | A trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9 of this Schedule where—
-- src:3134 | (a) the sole reason for paragraph 9 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees, and
-- src:3135 | (b) less than two years have passed since that person’s death.
@ref sch 3A para 9+1 (src:3133-3135)
GIVEN `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sole reason for paragraph 9 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the death of that trustee` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 9+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9 within two years of a trustee's death` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9`
           AND `the sole reason for paragraph 9 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees`
           AND `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of that trustee` `the date for which the trust is being tested`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9`
           AND (NOT (    `the sole reason for paragraph 9 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees`
                     AND `sch 3A less than two years have passed since the death` `the date of the death of that trustee` `the date for which the trust is being tested`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9 of this Schedule where— (a) the sole reason for paragraph 9 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees, and (b) less than two years have passed since that person's death"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3136 | 9B Revocation of survivorship destination trusts
-- src:3137 | A trust created under a deed or instrument which—
-- src:3138 | (a) revokes a survivorship destination in respect of common property in Scotland; and
-- src:3139 | (b) provides that from the date of execution of the deed or instrument the common property is held in trust for the common owners equally between them and for their respective executors and assignees.
@ref sch 3A para 9B (src:3136-3139)
GIVEN `the trust was created under a deed or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed or instrument revokes a survivorship destination in respect of common property in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deed or instrument provides that from the date of execution the common property is held in trust for the common owners equally between them and for their respective executors and assignees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 9B the trust is a trust created under a deed revoking a survivorship destination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust was created under a deed or instrument`
            AND `the deed or instrument revokes a survivorship destination in respect of common property in Scotland`
            AND `the deed or instrument provides that from the date of execution the common property is held in trust for the common owners equally between them and for their respective executors and assignees`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3140 | 10 Financial markets infrastructure
-- src:3141 | (1) A trust—
-- src:3142 | (a) created under, or for the purpose of, the default arrangements of a designated system or of the default rules of a recognised body, or for the purpose of any action or proceedings taken by or for such a system or body under such arrangements or rules;
-- src:3143 | (b) relating to the creation of a beneficial interest in securities belonging to a person whose name and address are maintained on a register of securities (within the meaning of regulation 3(1) of the Uncertificated Securities Regulations 2001); or
-- src:3144 | (c) created by or for a segregating entity—
-- src:3145 | (i) for the purpose of protecting sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity’s clients; or
-- src:3146 | (ii) for the purpose of complying with a legal obligation to safeguard and segregate sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity’s clients or to keep separate client records and accounts.
@ref sch 3A para 10(1) (src:3140-3146)
GIVEN `the trust was created under, or for the purpose of, the default arrangements of a designated system or of the default rules of a recognised body, or for the purpose of any action or proceedings taken by or for such a system or body under such arrangements or rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust relates to the creation of a beneficial interest in securities belonging to a person whose name and address are maintained on a register of securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a participant in a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a recognised body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purpose of complying with a legal obligation to safeguard and segregate sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients or to keep separate client records and accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 10(1) the trust is a financial markets infrastructure trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust was created under, or for the purpose of, the default arrangements of a designated system or of the default rules of a recognised body, or for the purpose of any action or proceedings taken by or for such a system or body under such arrangements or rules`
            OR `the trust relates to the creation of a beneficial interest in securities belonging to a person whose name and address are maintained on a register of securities`
            OR (    `sch 3A para 10(2) the entity is a segregating entity` `the entity is an authorised person` `the entity is a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty` `the entity is a participant in a designated system` `the entity is a designated system` `the entity is a recognised body` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                AND (    `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients`
                      OR `the trust was created for the purpose of complying with a legal obligation to safeguard and segregate sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients or to keep separate client records and accounts`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `sch 3A para 10(2) the entity is a segregating entity` `the entity is an authorised person` `the entity is a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty` `the entity is a participant in a designated system` `the entity is a designated system` `the entity is a recognised body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND (    `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients`
                      OR `the trust was created for the purpose of complying with a legal obligation to safeguard and segregate sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients or to keep separate client records and accounts`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'segregating entity' means— an authorised person; a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty; a participant in a designated system; a designated system; or a recognised body": limb (c) turns on a term defined with "means", and its no passes through when the trust is (c)-shaped (a purpose of (c)(i) or (c)(ii)); limbs (a) and (b) above are tried first (assumed, not ruled: FORK S3A-F7)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3147 | (2) In this paragraph—
-- src:3148 | “clearing member” and “default rules” have the meanings given, respectively, in sections 190(1) and 188 of the Companies Act 1989;
-- src:3149 | “default arrangements”, “designated system” and “participant” have the meanings given in regulation 2(1) of the Financial Markets and Insolvency (Settlement Finality) Regulations 1999;
-- src:3150 | “recognised body” and “recognised central counterparty” have the meanings given in section 313 of FSMA;
-- src:3151 | “segregating entity” means—
-- src:3152 | an authorised person;
-- src:3153 | a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty;
-- src:3154 | a participant in a designated system;
-- src:3155 | a designated system; or
-- src:3156 | a recognised body.
@ref sch 3A para 10(2) (src:3147-3156)
GIVEN `the entity is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a participant in a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is a recognised body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 10(2) the entity is a segregating entity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the entity is an authorised person`
            OR `the entity is a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty`
            OR `the entity is a participant in a designated system`
            OR `the entity is a designated system`
            OR `the entity is a recognised body`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'segregating entity' means— an authorised person; a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty; a participant in a designated system; a designated system; or a recognised body"


-- The terms paragraph 10(2) borrows: "clearing member" and "default rules" have the meanings given, respectively,
-- in sections 190(1) and 188 of the Companies Act 1989; "default arrangements", "designated system" and "participant" in
-- regulation 2(1) of the Financial Markets and Insolvency (Settlement Finality) Regulations 1999; "recognised body" and
-- "recognised central counterparty" in section 313 of FSMA.  A pointer, word for word; the definitions are those
-- instruments' own.
DECLARE `sch 3A para 10(2) borrowed term` IS ONE OF
    `sch 3A para 10(2) clearing member`
    `sch 3A para 10(2) default rules`
    `sch 3A para 10(2) default arrangements`
    `sch 3A para 10(2) designated system`
    `sch 3A para 10(2) participant`
    `sch 3A para 10(2) recognised body`
    `sch 3A para 10(2) recognised central counterparty`

@ref sch 3A para 10(2) (src:3148-3150)
GIVEN term IS A `sch 3A para 10(2) borrowed term`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 3A para 10(2) the term has the meaning given by` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `sch 3A para 10(2) clearing member` THEN "section 190(1) of the Companies Act 1989"
    WHEN `sch 3A para 10(2) default rules` THEN "section 188 of the Companies Act 1989"
    WHEN `sch 3A para 10(2) default arrangements` THEN "regulation 2(1) of the Financial Markets and Insolvency (Settlement Finality) Regulations 1999"
    WHEN `sch 3A para 10(2) designated system` THEN "regulation 2(1) of the Financial Markets and Insolvency (Settlement Finality) Regulations 1999"
    WHEN `sch 3A para 10(2) participant` THEN "regulation 2(1) of the Financial Markets and Insolvency (Settlement Finality) Regulations 1999"
    WHEN `sch 3A para 10(2) recognised body` THEN "section 313 of FSMA"
    WHEN `sch 3A para 10(2) recognised central counterparty` THEN "section 313 of FSMA"

-- src:3157 | 11 Professional services
-- src:3158 | A trust created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of sums, assets or (in the case of sub-paragraph (c)), documents, belonging to a person other than the trustee, in connection with which sums, assets or documents the trustee is—
-- src:3159 | (a) carrying on by way of business the activity specified in article 40 (safeguarding and administering investments) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001;
-- src:3160 | (b) acting by way of business as the trustee of an authorised unit trust scheme (and for this purpose “trustee” and “authorised unit trust scheme” have the meanings given in section 237 of FSMA); or
-- src:3161 | (c) acting by way of business as an agent holding sums, assets or documents in escrow until the performance of a contractual condition agreed between two or more other persons, including the person for whom the sums, assets or documents are being held.
@ref sch 3A para 11 (src:3157-3161)
GIVEN `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of sums or assets belonging to a person other than the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of documents belonging to a person other than the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee is carrying on by way of business the activity specified in article 40 (safeguarding and administering investments) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee is acting by way of business as the trustee of an authorised unit trust scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee is acting by way of business as an agent holding sums, assets or documents in escrow until the performance of a contractual condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 11 the trust is a professional services trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (    (    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of sums or assets belonging to a person other than the trustee`
                     AND (    `the trustee is carrying on by way of business the activity specified in article 40 (safeguarding and administering investments) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001`
                           OR `the trustee is acting by way of business as the trustee of an authorised unit trust scheme`
                           OR `the trustee is acting by way of business as an agent holding sums, assets or documents in escrow until the performance of a contractual condition`))
                 OR (    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of documents belonging to a person other than the trustee`
                     AND `the trustee is acting by way of business as an agent holding sums, assets or documents in escrow until the performance of a contractual condition`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- Sub-paragraph (b): "trustee" and "authorised unit trust scheme" have the meanings given in section 237 of FSMA.
@ref sch 3A para 11(b) (src:3160)
DECLARE `sch 3A para 11(b) borrowed term` IS ONE OF
    `sch 3A para 11(b) trustee`
    `sch 3A para 11(b) authorised unit trust scheme`

@ref sch 3A para 11(b) (src:3160)
GIVEN term IS A `sch 3A para 11(b) borrowed term`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 3A para 11(b) the term has the meaning given by` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `sch 3A para 11(b) trustee` THEN "section 237 of FSMA"
    WHEN `sch 3A para 11(b) authorised unit trust scheme` THEN "section 237 of FSMA"

-- src:3162 | 12 Client money etc.
-- src:3163 | A trust created by a relevant supervised person for the purpose of holding client money, securities or other assets, where that trust is incidental to the carrying on of business by the relevant supervised person.
@ref sch 3A para 12 (src:3162-3163)
GIVEN `the creator is a relevant supervised person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purpose of holding client money, securities or other assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust is incidental to the carrying on of business by the relevant supervised person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 12 the trust is a client money trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the creator is a relevant supervised person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the trust was created for the purpose of holding client money, securities or other assets`
           AND `the trust is incidental to the carrying on of business by the relevant supervised person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the creator is a relevant supervised person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant supervised person' means— (a) a relevant person; or (b) a person who is subject to requirements ... and supervised ...": the head says "created by a relevant supervised person", a term defined with "means", so the definition's no passes through
        IF     `the creator is a relevant supervised person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the trust was created for the purpose of holding client money, securities or other assets`
           AND (NOT `the trust is incidental to the carrying on of business by the relevant supervised person`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where that trust is incidental to the carrying on of business by the relevant supervised person"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3164 | 13 Capital markets etc.
-- src:3165 | A trust created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating an activity listed in points 2, 3, 6, 7 or 8 of ... Schedule 2, or for protecting or enforcing rights relating to that activity, where—
-- src:3166 | (a) one or more of the participants in that activity is a relevant supervised person, and
-- src:3167 | (b) the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of that activity.
@ref sch 3A para 13 (src:3164-3167)
GIVEN `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating an activity listed in points 2, 3, 6, 7 or 8 of Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to that activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more of the participants in that activity is a relevant supervised person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of that activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 13 the trust is a capital markets trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating an activity listed in points 2, 3, 6, 7 or 8 of Schedule 2`
                 OR `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to that activity`)
           AND `one or more of the participants in that activity is a relevant supervised person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of that activity`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     (    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating an activity listed in points 2, 3, 6, 7 or 8 of Schedule 2`
                 OR `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to that activity`)
           AND (    `one or more of the participants in that activity is a relevant supervised person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                 OR (NOT `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of that activity`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where— (a) one or more of the participants in that activity is a relevant supervised person, and (b) the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of that activity"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3168 | 14 Commercial transactions
-- src:3169 | A trust created for the purpose of—
-- src:3170 | (a) enabling or facilitating a transaction effected for genuine commercial reasons; or
-- src:3171 | (b) protecting or enforcing rights relating to such a transaction,
-- src:3172 | where the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of the transaction.
@ref sch 3A para 14 (src:3168-3172)
GIVEN `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating a transaction effected for genuine commercial reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to such a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 14 the trust is a commercial transactions trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating a transaction effected for genuine commercial reasons`
                 OR `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to such a transaction`)
           AND `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of the transaction`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     (    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating a transaction effected for genuine commercial reasons`
                 OR `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to such a transaction`)
           AND (NOT `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of the transaction`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust created for the purpose of— (a) enabling or facilitating a transaction effected for genuine commercial reasons; or (b) protecting or enforcing rights relating to such a transaction, where the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of the transaction"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3173 | 15 Registration of assets
-- src:3174 | A trust created on the transfer or disposal of an asset where the purpose of the trust is to hold the legal title to the asset on trust for the person to whom the transfer or disposal is being made until the time when the procedure required by law to effect the transfer or disposal of legal title is completed.
@ref sch 3A para 15 (src:3173-3174)
GIVEN `the trust was created on the transfer or disposal of an asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the trust is to hold the legal title to the asset on trust for the person to whom the transfer or disposal is being made until the procedure required by law to effect the transfer or disposal of legal title is completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 15 the trust is a registration of assets trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust was created on the transfer or disposal of an asset`
           AND `the purpose of the trust is to hold the legal title to the asset on trust for the person to whom the transfer or disposal is being made until the procedure required by law to effect the transfer or disposal of legal title is completed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the trust was created on the transfer or disposal of an asset`
           AND (NOT `the purpose of the trust is to hold the legal title to the asset on trust for the person to whom the transfer or disposal is being made until the procedure required by law to effect the transfer or disposal of legal title is completed`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trust created on the transfer or disposal of an asset where the purpose of the trust is to hold the legal title to the asset on trust for the person to whom the transfer or disposal is being made until the time when the procedure required by law to effect the transfer or disposal of legal title is completed"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3175 | 16 Trusts meeting legislative requirements
-- src:3176 | A trust holding property to which section 71A or 71D of the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 applies.
@ref sch 3A para 16 (src:3175-3176)
GIVEN `the trust holds property to which section 71A or 71D of the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 16 the trust holds property to which section 71A or 71D of the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust holds property to which section 71A or 71D of the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 applies`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3177 | A trust of property in respect of which a direction under paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 has effect.
@ref sch 3A para 16+1 (src:3177)
GIVEN `the trust is of property in respect of which a direction under paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 has effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 16+1 the trust is of property subject to a direction under paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Inheritance Tax Act 1984` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust is of property in respect of which a direction under paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 has effect`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3178 | A trust of funds derived from a payment—
-- src:3179 | (a) made for the benefit of a person in consequence of a personal injury to that person, and
-- src:3180 | (b) disregarded from capital under regulation 46(2) of, and paragraph 12 of Schedule 10 to, the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987.
@ref sch 3A para 16+2 (src:3178-3180)
GIVEN `the trust is of funds derived from a payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment was made for the benefit of a person in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment was disregarded from capital under regulation 46(2) of, and paragraph 12 of Schedule 10 to, the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 16+2 the trust is a trust of funds derived from a personal injury payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust is of funds derived from a payment`
            AND `the payment was made for the benefit of a person in consequence of a personal injury to that person`
            AND `the payment was disregarded from capital under regulation 46(2) of, and paragraph 12 of Schedule 10 to, the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3181 | A trust holding tenants’ contributions for the purposes of section 42 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1987.
@ref sch 3A para 16+3 (src:3181)
GIVEN `the trust holds tenants' contributions for the purposes of section 42 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1987` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 16+3 the trust holds tenants' contributions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust holds tenants' contributions for the purposes of section 42 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1987`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3182 | The plan trust of a share incentive plan which meets the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003.
@ref sch 3A para 16+4 (src:3182)
GIVEN `the trust is the plan trust of a share incentive plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share incentive plan meets the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 16+4 the trust is the plan trust of a share incentive plan` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust is the plan trust of a share incentive plan`
            AND `the share incentive plan meets the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3183 | A trust created under a share option scheme that meets the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003.
@ref sch 3A para 16+5 (src:3183)
GIVEN `the trust was created under a share option scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share option scheme meets the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 16+5 the trust is created under a share option scheme` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust was created under a share option scheme`
            AND `the share option scheme meets the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3184 | A trust holding property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005.
@ref sch 3A para 16+6 (src:3184)
GIVEN `the trust holds property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 16+6 the trust holds property for a disabled beneficiary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trust holds property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3185 | 23 Public authorities
-- src:3186 | A trust created for the purposes of enabling or assisting—
-- src:3187 | (a) a public authority, within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000, or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act;
-- src:3188 | (b) a Scottish public authority, within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002;
-- src:3189 | (c) the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency; or
-- src:3190 | (d) the Welsh Assembly Government,
-- src:3191 | to carry out its functions, including any functions as a court or tribunal and, in the case of the Bank of England, any of its functions as a monetary authority within the meaning of section 244(2)(c) of the Banking Act 2009.
@ref sch 3A para 23 (src:3185-3191)
GIVEN `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to carry out its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 23 the trust is a public authorities trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     (    `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act`
                 OR `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002`
                 OR `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency`
                 OR `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government`)
           AND `the purpose is to carry out its functions`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3192 | 23A General exclusion
-- src:3193 | (1) A trust which—
-- src:3194 | (a) does not hold any interest in land in the United Kingdom;
-- src:3195 | (b) does not hold assets of appreciable worth with a value exceeding £2,000 in total;
-- src:3196 | (c) has not held property with a cumulative total value exceeding £10,000 since the date on which it was created; and
-- src:3197 | (d) does not have an income exceeding £5,000 per annum.
-- src:3198 | (2) This paragraph does not apply to a trust which is a UK trust which is an express trust where—
-- src:3199 | (a) the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts, and
-- src:3200 | (b) one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph (a) is or was an excluded trust under this paragraph.
@ref sch 3A para 23A (src:3192-3200)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3A para 23A(1)(b) the ceiling on assets of appreciable worth in pounds` MEANS 2000

@ref sch 3A para 23A(1)(c) (src:3196)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3A para 23A(1)(c) the ceiling on cumulative value held in pounds` MEANS 10000

@ref sch 3A para 23A(1)(d) (src:3197)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3A para 23A(1)(d) the ceiling on income per annum in pounds` MEANS 5000

@ref sch 3A para 23A (src:3192-3200)
GIVEN `the trust holds an interest in land in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total value of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds` IS A NUMBER
      `the cumulative total value of the property the trust has held since it was created` IS A NUMBER
      `the income of the trust per annum` IS A NUMBER
      `the trust is a UK trust which is an express trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph 23A(2)(a) is or was an excluded trust under paragraph 23A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 23A the trust is within the general exclusion` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the trust is a UK trust which is an express trust`
           AND `the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts`
           AND `one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph 23A(2)(a) is or was an excluded trust under paragraph 23A`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph does not apply to a trust which is a UK trust which is an express trust where (a) the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts, and (b) one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph (a) is or was an excluded trust under this paragraph"
        IF     (NOT `the trust holds an interest in land in the United Kingdom`)
           AND `the total value of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds` AT MOST `sch 3A para 23A(1)(b) the ceiling on assets of appreciable worth in pounds`
           AND `the cumulative total value of the property the trust has held since it was created` AT MOST `sch 3A para 23A(1)(c) the ceiling on cumulative value held in pounds`
           AND `the income of the trust per annum` AT MOST `sch 3A para 23A(1)(d) the ceiling on income per annum in pounds`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph describes one kind of trust that is an excluded trust and does not say that a trust outside the description is not one


-- src:3201 | (3) In this paragraph, “assets of appreciable worth” includes works of art, antiques, collectibles, jewellery and other non-financial assets capable of increasing in value over time.
@ref sch 3A para 23A(3) (src:3201)
GIVEN `the kind of asset` IS A `sch 3A kind of asset`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 23A(3) the asset is an asset of appreciable worth` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of asset`
    WHEN `sch 3A a work of art` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3A an antique` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3A a collectible` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3A jewellery` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3A another non-financial asset capable of increasing in value over time` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3A an asset of another kind` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes works of art, antiques, collectibles, jewellery and other non-financial assets capable of increasing in value over time" opens the list; an asset of another kind is not said to be outside it


-- src:3202 | 24 Interpretation
-- src:3203 | In this Schedule, “relevant supervised person” means—
-- src:3204 | (a) a relevant person; or
-- src:3205 | (b) a person who is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive) and supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive.
@ref sch 3A para 24 (src:3202-3205)
GIVEN `the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A para 24 the person is a relevant supervised person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            OR (    `the person is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity`
                AND `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND (NOT (    `the person is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity`
                     AND `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive`))
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant supervised person' means— (a) a relevant person; or (b) a person who is subject to requirements ... and supervised ..."
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a relevant person (limb (a)) has not been answered, and limb (b) is not met


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B, as guidance for gathering a legal effect's routes by hand only; every
-- paragraph also has its own function above, option C).  No construct that gathers by name is used.
--
-- All the facts of all the paragraphs, as one record, so that the gathered question can be asked of one trust.
-- A fact that a paragraph does not read is simply not read.  The same fact asked in two paragraphs (the date for
-- which the trust is tested, the date of a death, a deed or instrument, the facts about a bank, the facts about
-- an entity) is one field.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `sch 3A facts about the trust` HAS
    `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the death of that trustee` IS A DATE
    `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS A DATE
    `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is of a life policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS A `Part of the United Kingdom`
    `the trust is registered as a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of the property the trust holds` IS A NUMBER
    `the date the trust was created` IS A DATE
    `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS A DATE
    `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was effected by will` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was beneficially entitled to all the property the trust holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the death of the person` IS A DATE
    `the trust holds only benefits received on the death of the person assured under a policy within paragraph 4` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created under a deed or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deed or instrument varies any of the dispositions of property comprised in the estate on death of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deed or instrument was made by the persons or any of the persons who benefit or would benefit from the dispositions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is of jointly held property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustees and the beneficiaries are the same persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 9` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sole reason for paragraph 9 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deed or instrument revokes a survivorship destination in respect of common property in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deed or instrument provides that from the date of execution the common property is held in trust for the common owners equally between them and for their respective executors and assignees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created under, or for the purpose of, the default arrangements of a designated system or of the default rules of a recognised body, or for the purpose of any action or proceedings taken by or for such a system or body under such arrangements or rules` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust relates to the creation of a beneficial interest in securities belonging to a person whose name and address are maintained on a register of securities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entity is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entity is a clearing member of a recognised central counterparty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entity is a participant in a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entity is a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entity is a recognised body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of complying with a legal obligation to safeguard and segregate sums or assets belonging to the segregating entity's clients or to keep separate client records and accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of sums or assets belonging to a person other than the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating the holding of documents belonging to a person other than the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee is carrying on by way of business the activity specified in article 40 (safeguarding and administering investments) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee is acting by way of business as the trustee of an authorised unit trust scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee is acting by way of business as an agent holding sums, assets or documents in escrow until the performance of a contractual condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the creator is a relevant supervised person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of holding client money, securities or other assets` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is incidental to the carrying on of business by the relevant supervised person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating an activity listed in points 2, 3, 6, 7 or 8 of Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to that activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one or more of the participants in that activity is a relevant supervised person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of that activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of enabling or facilitating a transaction effected for genuine commercial reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purpose of protecting or enforcing rights relating to such a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the use of the trust is incidental to the principal purpose of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created on the transfer or disposal of an asset` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose of the trust is to hold the legal title to the asset on trust for the person to whom the transfer or disposal is being made until the procedure required by law to effect the transfer or disposal of legal title is completed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust holds property to which section 71A or 71D of the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is of property in respect of which a direction under paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Inheritance Tax Act 1984 has effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is of funds derived from a payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment was made for the benefit of a person in consequence of a personal injury to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment was disregarded from capital under regulation 46(2) of, and paragraph 12 of Schedule 10 to, the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust holds tenants' contributions for the purposes of section 42 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1987` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is the plan trust of a share incentive plan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the share incentive plan meets the requirements of Part 9 of Schedule 2 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created under a share option scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the share option scheme meets the requirements of Parts 2 to 7 of Schedule 3 to the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust holds property for a beneficiary who is a disabled person within the meaning given by Schedule 1A to the Finance Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 or a body specified in section 80(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting a Scottish public authority within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Freedom of Information (Scotland) Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Security Service, the Secret Intelligence Service, the Government Communications Headquarters or the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust was created for the purposes of enabling or assisting the Welsh Assembly Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose is to carry out its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust holds an interest in land in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total value of the assets of appreciable worth that the trust holds` IS A NUMBER
    `the cumulative total value of the property the trust has held since it was created` IS A NUMBER
    `the income of the trust per annum` IS A NUMBER
    `the trust is a UK trust which is an express trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the settlor has, during his or her lifetime, created one or more other UK trusts which are express trusts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of the trusts mentioned in paragraph 23A(2)(a) is or was an excluded trust under paragraph 23A` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A relevant-supervised-person answer that is not yet known (NOTHING) is read as yes, to ask what the paragraphs would say if it were.
GIVEN answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A treat an unknown answer as yes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF answer EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE answer

-- The answers of the paragraphs, gathered.  JUST TRUE if any paragraph says the trust is of its kind.  Otherwise NOTHING if a paragraph would say so were an unknown
-- relevant-supervised-person answer (paragraphs 12 and 13) to turn out yes.  Otherwise JUST FALSE: the term "a trust listed in Schedule 3A (excluded trusts)" of
-- regulations 42, 45 and 45ZA is read as handed to the list of paragraphs, so that a trust within no paragraph is not listed (assumed, not ruled: FORK S3A-F8;
-- Meng's ruling of 2026-11-05 on a definition handed to a list).  The paragraphs that answer NOTHING for a trust outside their description (the relative-clause paragraphs of FORK S3A-F2)
-- do not make this answer NOTHING.
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `answers if the unknown answers were yes` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A the answers of the paragraphs, gathered` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) answers
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) `answers if the unknown answers were yes`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the creator of the trust, or a participant in the activity, is a relevant supervised person has not been answered, and a yes would make paragraph 12 or 13 say that the trust is excluded
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the term "a trust listed in Schedule 3A (excluded trusts)" is read as handed to the Schedule's list of paragraphs (Meng's ruling of 2026-11-05 on a definition handed to a list; assumed to apply here, FORK S3A-F8), and no paragraph says the trust is of its kind

-- SEAM S-18 (answering): part mlr2, regs 42, 45(10A) and 45ZA, asks `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`;
-- the merge replaces its input with a call to this function.
@ref sch 3A (paragraphs 1 to 24 together)
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 3A facts about the trust`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A` MEANS
    `sch 3A the answers of the paragraphs, gathered`
        (LIST (`sch 3A para 1 the trust is a legislative trust` WITH `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment` IS facts's `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment`)
            , (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS facts's `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1`, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS facts's `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925`, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS facts's `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees`, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS facts's `the date of the death of that trustee`, `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS facts's `the date for which the trust is being tested`)
            , (`sch 3A para 2 the trust is a trust imposed by court order` WITH `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal` IS facts's `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal`)
            , (`sch 3A para 3 the trust is a pension scheme trust` WITH `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme` IS facts's `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme`, `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004` IS facts's `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004`)
            , (`sch 3A para 4(1) the trust is a trust of a life policy paying out only on the listed events or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of a life policy` IS facts's `the trust is of a life policy`, `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)` IS facts's `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)`)
            , (`sch 3A para 4(2) the trust is a trust of an insurance policy paying out only on temporary disablement or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS facts's `the trust is of an insurance policy`, `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS facts's `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured`, `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS facts's `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)`, `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS facts's `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)`)
            , (`sch 3A para 4(3) the trust is a trust of the death benefits of a retirement policy` WITH `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy` IS facts's `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy`)
